    [Doc][Misc] Clarify EPLB hardware and redundant expert constraints (#18887)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    This is a documentation-only update for EPLB.
    
    It clarifies the supported hardware and redundant-expert constraints,
    including:
    
    - A2 does not support redundant experts; `num_redundant_experts` must be
    set to `0` on A2.
    - `num_redundant_experts` is only applicable to hardware that supports
    redundant experts.
    - Clarifies the supported weight formats and validation status for Model
    Runner V2.
    - Fixes the Qwen3-235B model name to `Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B`.
    - Corrects the Markdown diagram fence and restores the MRv1 parameter
    table.
    - Uses the repository MkDocs admonition format.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This is a documentation update only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Ran `git diff --check`.
    - Verified the modified Markdown structure locally.
    - Documentation CI will validate Markdown formatting and links.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
